            <ArticleTitle>[Temporo-spheno-orbital meningioma. An unusual cause of exophthalmos. Report of one case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 48-year-old woman with no prior medical history who developed headache and unilateral exophthalmos for 6 months. Clinical and radiographic findings detailed the intracranial extension of a temporo-spheno-orbital meningioma. Histological diagnosis was established after curative neurosurgery. This case recalls the characteristic features of temporo-spheno-orbital meningiomas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
